<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Wild-Olive-Final-2.jpg" alt="Plein air painting featuring a Russian olive tree, pines and an open grassy field." width="497" height="376" /></p>
<p>This is my first plein air of the 2013 season.</p>
<p>I actually painted this over several days (it's my own back yard, so visiting the location multiple times isn't a problem). &nbsp;I first made a preliminary sketch then I used it to help develop a more interesting composition and better color selection. &nbsp;A couple of days later I went back to the same spot and painted the whole thing in one session on a fresh canvas. &nbsp;After that was dry I re-worked the center of interest, filled out the foreground and pushed the trees on the right further back.</p>
<p>After looking at the painting for a few days back in the studio I decided that the sky was too busy for the scene and repainted it.&nbsp;</p>
<p>"Wild Olive" 14x18 oil on linen.</p>